// A runaway recursion used to make reporting the error cost more than the recursion did. build_trace
// allocated a fresh buffer and copied the whole trace for every one of ~152,000 frames -- quadratic
// -- so this program took 402 seconds, 1.97 GB of RSS and 198,578 lines of stderr, of which 23,170
// were Boehm complaining about the repeated huge allocations (nothing had ever called
// GC_set_warn_proc). In a server that is a denial of service reachable from any input that can drive
// recursion. The buffer now grows by doubling and the trace prints the innermost 32 frames, a count
// of what was left out, and the outermost 8: an 8 MB error message is useless even when produced
// quickly. Takes about two seconds now, so this fixture also guards the harness timeout.
fn deep(n: int) -> int {
    return deep(n + 1)
}

fn main() {
    print(deep(0))
}
